  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Suppose \\(A,\\) \\(B,\\) and \\(C\\) are three numbers for which \\(1001C-2002A=4004\\) and \\(1001B+3003A=5005.\\) The average of the three numbers \\(A,\\) \\(B,\\) and \\(C\\) is",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(6\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(9\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "not uniquely determined"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": "3"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2002-p9.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Adding the equations, \\[ \\begin{gathered} 1001C-2002A+1001B \\\\ {}+3003A \\\\ = 1001A+1001B+1001C \\\\ = 9009. \\end{gathered} \\]\n\nSo \\(A+B+C=9\\) and the average is \\(\\dfrac{9}{3}=3.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Add the two equations together",
        "The sum collapses to a multiple of \\(A+B+C\\)"
      ],
